# THE CONTEXT HUB — .claude/ consolidation policy
# Established 2026-08-16. Audit and re-consolidate on a regular basis.
# ============================================================


# POLICY. Claude Code creates a .claude/ wherever it is started. Two kinds of
# thing land there and they have OPPOSITE homes:
#
#   CONTENT   scratchpad/, commands/, notes, READMEs
#             -> CENTRALISE into $CONTEXT_HUB. Portable, no CWD dependency.
#
#   CONFIG    settings.json, settings.local.json
#             -> MUST STAY. Claude Code resolves these relative to the startup
#                directory. Moving them silently drops that project's
#                permissions and plugins. This is not a preference.
#
#   MEMORY    MEMORY.md and memory/*.md
#             -> LEAVE PARTITIONED, deliberately. Per-work-directory memory is
#                more useful where it landed than in a hub. Directory-specific
#                facts stay local; anything that transcends a directory is
#                promoted to the ThePlace-level memory.
#                NOTE: these live under ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/,
#                NOT inside ThePlace. There are zero MEMORY.md files in the
#                ThePlace tree itself (verified 2026-08-16).

